---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailSubject = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=UGC%20Ads%20production%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20brand";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="UGC Ads — The Complete Guide to Creator-Made Paid Advertising | OKAD"
  description="UGC Ads use authentic creator-made content as paid advertising. They get 4x higher CTR and ~50% lower CPC than brand-produced ads. This guide covers ad types, platforms, metrics, briefing, and scaling."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          UGC Ads: <span class="text-accent">The Complete Guide</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          UGC Ads use authentic creator-made content as paid advertising. They look native, not like ads &mdash; and they outperform polished brand creative on every metric that matters. This guide covers everything you need to run UGC ads at scale.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailSubject} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Order UGC ad creatives &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>4x higher CTR</span>
          <span>~50% lower CPC</span>
          <span>Meta &amp; TikTok</span>
          <span>Vertical video</span>
          <span>Hook &rarr; CTA</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">Why UGC Ads Outperform</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4F1;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Native Feel</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">UGC ads look like organic content, not ads. Vertical video, raw aesthetic, real people. The viewer watches before they realize it's an ad.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4CA;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">4x Higher CTR</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">UGC ads consistently achieve 4x higher click-through rates and ~50% lower cost per click than brand-produced ad creative.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F50D;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Test &amp; Scale</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Produce 10-20 UGC ad variants, test all of them, kill losers fast, and scale spend on the winners. Volume is the strategy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "What Are UGC Ads?", href: "#what" },
            { num: "03", text: "UGC Ad Types", href: "#types" },
            { num: "04", text: "UGC Ads vs Brand Ads", href: "#comparison" },
            { num: "05", text: "Ad Structure & Scripting", href: "#structure" },
            { num: "06", text: "Platforms & Placements", href: "#platforms" },
            { num: "07", text: "Metrics & Benchmarks", href: "#metrics" },
            { num: "08", text: "How to Brief Creators", href: "#briefing" },
            { num: "09", text: "Common Mistakes", href: "#mistakes" },
            { num: "10", text: "Glossary", href: "#glossary" },
            { num: "11", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Creator-made content as paid advertising</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">UGC ads = using creator-produced video as paid ad creative</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">4x higher CTR, ~50% lower CPC than brand-produced ads</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">They work because they look native &mdash; not like ads</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">UGC Ads are paid advertisements that use creator-made content instead of brand-produced creative. A real person &mdash; not a studio, not a model &mdash; films a video about a product, and the brand runs it as a paid ad on Meta, TikTok, or YouTube. The content looks and feels like something a friend posted, not like a commercial.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This is the dominant paid creative format in 2026. The data is unambiguous: UGC ads achieve roughly 4x higher click-through rates and approximately 50% lower cost per click than polished brand creative. They outperform because they bypass the viewer's ad filter &mdash; they look like organic content in the feed.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">UGC ads are not influencer marketing. The creator's audience is irrelevant. The brand buys the content, not the reach. The ad runs from the brand's ad account (or via <a href="/ugc-whitelisting" class="text-accent hover:underline">whitelisting</a> from the creator's account), targeting the brand's chosen audiences. The creator is a production resource, not a distribution channel.</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Format:</strong> vertical video (9:16), 15&ndash;60 seconds</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Performance:</strong> 4x CTR, ~50% lower CPC vs brand ads</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Platforms:</strong> Meta (Reels, Stories, Feed), TikTok, YouTube Shorts</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Budget:</strong> start at $1K&ndash;$5K/month testing budget</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 What Are UGC Ads -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="what">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Definition</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What are UGC ads?</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Paid ads using creator-filmed content instead of brand-produced creative</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The ad looks like organic content &mdash; raw, authentic, vertical</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Not influencer marketing &mdash; the brand buys the content, not the audience</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>UGC Ads</strong> are paid advertisements built on creator-made content. A brand commissions a creator to film a video &mdash; a testimonial, a demo, an unboxing, a reaction &mdash; and then runs that video as a paid ad. The creative looks native to the platform: vertical video, phone-filmed aesthetic, real person talking to the camera.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">A quick example</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A skincare brand pays a creator $250 to film a 30-second video talking about their morning routine and how the brand's moisturizer changed their skin. The creator films it on their phone, in their bathroom, in natural light. The brand takes that video, adds captions, and runs it as a paid ad on Instagram Reels targeting women 25&ndash;34. The ad gets a 2.1% CTR &mdash; triple what their studio-shot ads achieve.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Why UGC ads outperform</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Trust</strong> &mdash; viewers trust real people more than brands. A creator saying "I love this product" is more credible than a brand saying "You'll love our product."</li>
          <li><strong>Native feel</strong> &mdash; UGC ads look like content, not ads. They blend into the feed. Viewers watch them before the ad filter kicks in.</li>
          <li><strong>Social proof</strong> &mdash; a real person using a real product is implicit social proof. Someone like them already bought it and likes it.</li>
          <li><strong>Lower production cost</strong> &mdash; a creator films on their phone for $150&ndash;$500 per video. A brand studio shoot costs $5K&ndash;$50K+. UGC lets you produce 10&ndash;20 variants for the price of one studio ad.</li>
          <li><strong>Testing volume</strong> &mdash; because production cost is low, you can test more creative variations. More tests = faster learning = better performance.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What UGC ads are not</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Not influencer marketing</strong> &mdash; the creator's follower count and audience are irrelevant. The brand buys content, not distribution.</li>
          <li><strong>Not organic UGC</strong> &mdash; these are paid ads. The brand controls targeting, budget, and placement. The creator just provides the creative.</li>
          <li><strong>Not low-quality content</strong> &mdash; "authentic" does not mean "sloppy." UGC ads require clear audio, good lighting, and a tight script. They just don't look like studio productions.</li>
          <li><strong>Not <a href="/canvas-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC</a></strong> &mdash; in Canvas UGC, creators post on brand accounts organically. UGC ads are paid media using creator content.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 UGC Ad Types -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="types">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; Ad Types</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Types of UGC ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Testimonial, demo, unboxing, before/after, reaction</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Each type serves a different stage of the buyer journey</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Test multiple types &mdash; you can't predict which wins</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Ad Type</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">What it is</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Best for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Testimonial ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator talks about their personal experience with the product</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Trust building, mid-funnel</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Demo ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator shows the product in use, demonstrates features or workflow</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Tech products, SaaS, apps</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Unboxing ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator opens and reacts to the product for the first time</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Physical products, DTC, beauty</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Before/after ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Shows the transformation &mdash; life before the product vs after</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Fitness, skincare, productivity tools</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Reaction ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator reacts to results, features, or a surprising product moment</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Viral hooks, top-of-funnel awareness</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Problem/solution ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator describes a pain point, then introduces the product as the fix</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Any product with a clear use case</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Routine/day-in-life ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Product shown naturally within the creator's daily routine</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Lifestyle products, supplements, apps</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Comparison ad</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Creator compares the product to an alternative or the old way</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Competitive positioning, switching</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Choosing the right type</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Different ad types work for different funnel stages and product categories. Testimonials build trust for mid-funnel retargeting. Demo ads work best for tech products where the viewer needs to see the interface. Unboxing ads create excitement for physical products. Reaction ads generate curiosity for top-of-funnel prospecting.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The best approach: don't choose one type. Order 10&ndash;20 videos across multiple types, test them all, and let performance data tell you which types work for your specific product and audience. This is <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">creative testing</a> &mdash; and it's the core of modern performance marketing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 UGC Ads vs Brand Ads -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="comparison">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Comparison</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">UGC ads vs brand ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand ads are studio-produced; UGC ads are creator-filmed</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">UGC wins on CTR, CPC, trust, and production speed</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand ads still work for brand awareness at scale</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Aspect</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Brand Ads</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">UGC Ads</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Look &amp; feel</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Polished, studio-quality, branded</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Raw, authentic, native to the feed</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CTR (click-through rate)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">0.3&ndash;0.8% typical</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">1&ndash;2% typical (4x higher)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CPC (cost per click)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Higher &mdash; ad filter reduces engagement</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">~50% lower than brand ads</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Production cost</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">$5K&ndash;$50K+ per shoot</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">$150&ndash;$500 per video</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Production time</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">2&ndash;6 weeks</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;7 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Variants per batch</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">1&ndash;3 per shoot</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">10&ndash;20+ per batch</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Trust signal</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brand authority</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Social proof, peer recommendation</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Best fit</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Brand awareness, upper funnel</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Performance marketing, direct response</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">UGC ads do not replace brand ads entirely. Brand creative still works for upper-funnel brand awareness campaigns, especially for established brands with strong visual identity. But for performance marketing &mdash; driving clicks, installs, purchases, and signups &mdash; UGC ads are the clear winner. Most brands in 2026 run a mix: UGC for direct response, brand creative for awareness.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Ad Structure & Scripting -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="structure">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Structure</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The anatomy of a UGC ad</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Structure: Hook &rarr; Problem &rarr; Solution &rarr; CTA</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The hook must stop the scroll in 1&ndash;3 seconds</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The CTA must be simple and direct &mdash; one action only</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The four-part framework</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Hook (0&ndash;3s).</strong> The single most important element. You have 1&ndash;3 seconds to stop the scroll. Use a surprising statement, a bold claim, a relatable frustration, or a visual pattern interrupt. "I spent $200 on skincare that didn't work until I tried this." "Stop paying for tools you don't use." The hook must be specific &mdash; vague hooks fail.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Problem (3&ndash;8s).</strong> Establish the pain point in 1&ndash;2 sentences. The viewer must recognize their own frustration. "I was spending 3 hours every week manually tracking expenses." "My skin was dry no matter what moisturizer I used." Keep it short &mdash; the viewer already knows the problem if the hook worked.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Solution (8&ndash;25s).</strong> Introduce and demonstrate the product. Show it working. For physical products: hold it, use it, show the result. For tech products: screen recording, app walkthrough, before/after. The viewer needs to see the product solving the problem stated in step 2. This is the body of the ad.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>CTA (final 2&ndash;5s).</strong> One clear action. "Link in bio." "Use code SAVE20." "Try it free &mdash; link below." Never stack multiple CTAs. The viewer should know exactly what to do next. Don't oversell &mdash; the demo already did the selling.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Hook formulas that work</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Contrarian</strong> &mdash; "Everyone told me not to buy this. They were wrong."</li>
          <li><strong>Outcome-first</strong> &mdash; "I lost 15 lbs in 3 months without changing my diet."</li>
          <li><strong>Direct address</strong> &mdash; "If you're still using spreadsheets to track leads, watch this."</li>
          <li><strong>Curiosity gap</strong> &mdash; "I found the product my dermatologist didn't want me to know about."</li>
          <li><strong>Social proof</strong> &mdash; "2 million people already use this and I finally see why."</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The hook determines 80% of the ad's performance. If viewers don't stop scrolling in the first 3 seconds, nothing else matters. Test multiple hooks against the same body &mdash; this is the fastest way to improve UGC ad performance.</p>
