        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What a UGC ad brief must include</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Product information.</strong> What the product is, what it does, who it's for, and what makes it different. Include a product sample or free account access. The creator must actually use the product before filming.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Hooks.</strong> Provide 3&ndash;5 hook options. Specific, concrete, tested if possible. "I tried 6 skincare brands before I found this one" is better than "Talk about how much you like the product."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Key messages.</strong> 2&ndash;3 talking points the creator should hit. Not a script &mdash; bullet points they can express in their own words. "Mention the 30-day money-back guarantee." "Show the before/after difference."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Tone and style.</strong> Casual? Energetic? Calm and informative? Include reference videos from other creators whose style matches what you want. "Like this, but for our product."</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Format and specs.</strong> Vertical 9:16. Duration range (15&ndash;45s). Whether to include captions. Whether face-to-camera or product-only. Ad type (testimonial, demo, unboxing).</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Do's and don'ts.</strong> What to avoid: mentioning competitors by name, making medical claims, showing competing products in frame. What to include: the product name (correct pronunciation), the CTA, any required disclosures.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 flex gap-4 items-start flex-col sm:flex-row">
          <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-[10px] bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] flex items-center justify-center text-[20px] shrink-0">&#9889;</div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-display text-[16px] font-semibold mb-1"><a href={emailSubject} class="text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors no-underline">OKAD writes briefs and manages creators for you</a></h4>
            <p class="text-[14px] text-muted m-0 leading-[1.5]">Our team handles the entire UGC ad production pipeline: creator matching, brief writing, quality review, revision management, and final delivery. You get ad-ready video files.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The over-scripting trap</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The most common briefing mistake: writing a word-for-word script and asking the creator to memorize it. This kills authenticity. The viewer can tell when someone is reading vs talking naturally. Give the creator talking points and let them deliver in their own voice. The slight imperfections &mdash; a pause, a natural filler word, a candid moment &mdash; are what make UGC ads feel real.</p>
