    <!-- 09 Common Mistakes -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="mistakes">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Mistakes</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Common mistakes with UGC ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Over-polishing destroys the native feel</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Testing too few variants = not enough data to learn</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">No clear CTA = views without conversions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Over-polishing.</strong> Adding motion graphics, transitions, brand intros, or color grading that makes the content look "produced." The whole point of UGC is that it looks like a real person's video, not a commercial. Leave the rough edges.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>No clear CTA.</strong> The viewer watched the whole ad but there's no specific action to take. "Check it out" is too vague. "Link in bio, 20% off with code SAVE20" is actionable. Every UGC ad needs exactly one clear CTA.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Testing too few variants.</strong> Ordering 2&ndash;3 UGC videos and expecting a winner. The realistic hit rate is 10&ndash;20%. You need 10&ndash;20 variants per month to find 1&ndash;3 winners. Volume is the testing strategy.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Weak hooks.</strong> Using generic openers like "So I just discovered this amazing product." The hook is 80% of the ad's performance. Invest time in writing multiple specific, concrete hooks for each brief.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Wrong creator fit.</strong> Choosing creators based on follower count instead of content quality and audience match. A creator with 500 followers who makes authentic content in your niche will outperform a creator with 500K followers in the wrong category.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Not iterating.</strong> Finding one winning ad and running it indefinitely. Creative fatigue sets in after 2&ndash;4 weeks. You need a constant pipeline of new UGC creative. Plan for ongoing production, not one-off batches.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Ignoring the data.</strong> Not analyzing which hooks, formats, and creator styles perform best. Each testing batch teaches you something. Track hook rate, CTR, and CPA by variant, and use the data to inform the next batch of briefs.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

