          { q: "What makes UGC ads perform better than brand ads?", a: "Four factors: trust (real people are more credible than brand messaging), native feel (UGC looks like organic content, bypassing the ad filter), social proof (someone like you already uses the product), and testing volume (low production cost means you can test 10-20 variants per batch instead of 1-3)." },
          { q: "How many UGC ad variants should I test per month?", a: "Minimum 10-20 variants per month. The realistic winner rate is 10-20% — meaning you need at least 10 variants to reliably find 1-2 winners. Test different hooks, formats, creator styles, and messaging angles. The more you test, the faster you learn what works." },
          { q: "What's the difference between UGC ads and influencer marketing?", a: "In influencer marketing, you pay for the creator's audience — they post to their followers. In UGC ads, you pay for the content — the creator films video and you run it as a paid ad targeting your own audiences. The creator's follower count is irrelevant in UGC ads." },
          { q: "What platforms work best for UGC ads?", a: "Meta (Instagram Reels, Stories, Feed) offers the largest scale and best targeting. TikTok is most native to the UGC format with strong discovery. YouTube Shorts is growing fast, especially for tech and educational content. Most brands test across all three platforms." },
          { q: "How long should a UGC ad be?", a: "15-60 seconds, with 15-30 seconds being the sweet spot for most placements. The hook (first 1-3 seconds) is far more important than overall length. A tight 15-second ad with a strong hook outperforms a 60-second ad with a weak opening." },
          { q: "What's the difference between UGC ads, whitelisting, and whitelabel UGC?", a: "UGC ads: creator films content, brand runs it as a paid ad from the brand's ad account. Whitelisting: brand runs paid ads from the creator's account for a more native look. Whitelabel UGC: creator delivers raw video files, brand edits and uses them however they want. All three use creator content — the difference is distribution and control." },
          { q: "How do I brief creators for UGC ads?", a: "Include: product information, 3-5 hook options, 2-3 key talking points, tone/style references, format specs (vertical, 15-45s), and do's/don'ts. Don't over-script — give talking points, not a teleprompter script. The creator's natural delivery is what makes UGC ads authentic." },
          { q: "Can OKAD produce UGC ads for my brand?", a: "Yes. We handle the entire UGC ad production pipeline: creator sourcing from our network, brief writing, production management, quality review, revisions, and delivery of ad-ready video files. We also offer whitelisting and creative testing services. Write to us at olga@okad.agency." },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="faq-item border-b border-border">
            <div class="faq-q flex justify-between items-center gap-4 py-5 cursor-pointer">
              <span class="font-display font-semibold text-[16px] text-ink">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[20px] text-accent shrink-0 faq-icon">+</span>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-a overflow-hidden max-h-0 transition-all duration-300">
              <div class="pb-5 text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-[1.65]">{item.a}</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Final CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(22px,3.5vw,32px)] tracking-[-0.02em] text-white mb-3">Ready to scale UGC ads?</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-muted max-w-[480px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-6">Tell us about your brand and your paid advertising goals. We'll produce UGC ad creative, manage creators, and deliver ad-ready video files every month.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
            <a href={emailSubject} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-white text-ink hover:bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Order UGC ad creatives &rarr;</a>
            <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold text-muted border border-white/15 hover:text-white hover:border-white/30 transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Methodology -->
    <section class="guide-section">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">Methodology</div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65]">This guide is based on observed UGC ad performance data, published platform benchmarks, and aggregate campaign results across multiple brands and categories. The 4x CTR and ~50% lower CPC figures reflect directional industry benchmarks for UGC vs brand-produced ad creative. Individual results depend on product quality, creative execution, audience targeting, and market conditions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-section {
    padding: 56px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .guide-section:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .tldr {
    background: rgba(99,102,241,.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(99,102,241,.12);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .guide-step {
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .guide-step::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 14px;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(99,102,241,.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(99,102,241,.15);
    color: #6366F1;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  ol:has(.guide-step) {
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .faq-item.open .faq-a {
    max-height: 500px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .guide-section { padding: 40px 0; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-q').forEach(q => {
    q.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const item = q.parentElement;
      if (!item) return;
      const isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
      item.classList.toggle('open');
      const icon = q.querySelector('.faq-icon');
      if (icon) icon.textContent = isOpen ? '+' : '−';
    });
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(a => {
    a.addEventListener('click', e => {
      const href = a.getAttribute('href');
      if (!href) return;
      const t = document.querySelector(href);
      if (t) { e.preventDefault(); t.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
    });
  });
</script>
